<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Colony wide bill list, alongside the other census tabs in the bottom button row.

    order 59 puts it between our grow zones tab (58) and vanilla's Research (60), so the tabs that answer
    "what is my colony doing" sit together.

    A workbench's own Bills tab is a different interface, not this window filtered. It used to be this one
    with a bench filter set, and that was wrong: clicking a bench answered a question about the whole colony
    and changed the tab bar underneath the player. See WorkBenchBillsTab.
  -->
  <MainButtonDef>
    <defName>Gideon_Bills</defName>
    <label>bills</label>
    <description>Every bill on every workbench in the colony: what it makes, how far along it is, who may work it, and which ones nobody can. Choose a bill to edit it in place, or save one as a template to reuse in any colony.</description>
    <tabWindowClass>Gideon.UIOverhaul.Features.Bills.MainTabWindow_Bills</tabWindowClass>
    <validWithoutMap>false</validWithoutMap>

    <!--
      No file extension and no Textures prefix: RimWorld's ContentFinder takes a path relative to Textures
      and appends the extension itself. An order slip with a cogwheel, 256 square in the same flat grayscale
      with a diagonal light to dark gradient as the rest of this mod's main button icons, so it tints with
      the palette the way the others do.

      A real file rather than a texture generated at run time, and that is the point rather than an
      implementation detail: the bar's own icon picker offers whatever it finds in a mod's
      Textures/UI/MainButtonIcons folder, and it stores the choice as a path. A generated texture has no
      path, so it could never be offered, reassigned or borrowed by another tab.
    -->
    <iconPath>UI/MainButtonIcons/Bills</iconPath>

    <order>59</order>
  </MainButtonDef>

</Defs>
